<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duarte Coelho</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1485–<a href="/years/1554">1554</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Duarte Coelho Pereira</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Duarte Coelho was a Portuguese soldier and navigator who had served in Asia before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> III granted him the captaincy of Pernambuco in 1534. Calling it Nova Lusitânia, he founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olinda">Olinda</a> and built a colony based on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> mills, which became the most prosperous of the hereditary captaincies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duarte-coelho.jpg" alt="Duarte Coelho" width="176" height="262" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Duarte-coelho-pereira-2-10-03-1534.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
